# Kconfig — techpack/camera/drivers/nd_controller
#
# ONE INCH WONDER — LC Variable ND Filter driver
# Xiaomi SM8550 (Kalama) camera techpack integration

config VIDEO_ND_CONTROLLER
	tristate "LC Variable ND Filter V4L2 subdev (One Inch Wonder)"
	depends on USB
	depends on VIDEO_V4L2
	depends on MEDIA_CONTROLLER
	depends on VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
	select V4L2_ASYNC
	help
	  Driver for the LCDRV-001 LC variable ND filter controller PCB
	  used in the One Inch Wonder project (Xiaomi 13U/14U + IMX989).

	  The board carries an STM32G0B1 MCU connected to the host via
	  USB CDC bulk endpoints.  The driver exposes ND attenuation,
	  operating mode, LC cell temperature, CCM index, and calibration
	  trigger as V4L2 subdev custom controls.

	  The subdev registers asynchronously (v4l2_async_register_subdev)
	  and is discovered by the Qualcomm camera service through the
	  shared media graph.  A board-level platform driver is responsible
	  for creating the media pad link between this subdev and the
	  IMX989 sensor entity.

	  To compile as a module, choose M — the module will be called
	  nd_controller.  It is safe to leave this as M even when the
	  Qualcomm camera stack is built-in.

	  If unsure, say M.
